import pathlib,json,datetime
root=pathlib.Path('/home/aither/workspace/ai/vpsfree.cz/work/2026-10-19-vpsadmin-kernel-cves/research');out=root/'platform-evidence';records={x['cve']:x for x in json.loads((root/'cve-evidence/range-records.json').read_text())}
entries=[
('80521','default_user','include','UNIX=y; own AF_UNIX socket/SCM_RIGHTS reference graph and close/send operations need no host capability or optional device. Default seccomp permits them.','SCC garbage-collector freed-vertex traversal; shared-kernel lifetime corruption. No platform-specific host escape verified.'),
('53388','default_tenant_admin','include','FUSE=m explicitly preloaded; /dev/fuse feature defaults on; downstream FUSE has FS_USERNS_MOUNT. Tenant admin can mount/operate own daemon and arrange request abort/copy lifecycle. Device permission and mount state are runtime facts.','fuse_io_args lifetime UAF; upstream .95 already contains this correction. Inclusive range selection does not mean .95 remains vulnerable.'),
('98041','unresolved_verifier_mitigation','defer','BPF syscalls/socket filters enabled, 6.12 source unprivileged_bpf_disabled=0. check_cond_jmp_op predicts immediate-zero pointer branch before final pointer-comparison rejection. However bypass_spec_v1=false invokes sanitize_speculative_path, which marks the compared register unknown and verifies the alternative branch. bpf_bypass_spec_v1 requires cpu_mitigations_off or token/initial CAP_PERFMON; ordinary userns root is insufficient.','The reviewed example cannot establish an ordinary unprivileged unsafe-memory path through speculative verification. Low-32-bit-zero pointer alignment and mitigation behavior remain prerequisites; no new exploit is tested. Keep conditional/unresolved rather than equating enabled BPF with a complete verifier bypass.'),
('98222','conditional_operator_module','conditional','KEYS=y, ENCRYPTED_KEYS=m; encrypted_keys absent from default preload. key_type_lookup searches registered types and returns ENOKEY if missing; it does not automatically provide the key type. Host module loading/activation needed under autoload-disabled defaults. Once registered, own encrypted-key creation is not intrinsically host-root-only.','Concrete integer truncation and large heap OOB write; no default tenant exposure claim while key type unregistered.'),
('63823','conditional_request_key_helper','defer','KEYS=y; request_key/keyctl permitted, but instantiate/reject paths require an actual request_key_auth instantiation permit. Source invokes host /sbin/request-key via usermode helper. A binary/configuration inside a tenant alone does not establish an attacker-accessible host helper/auth context. No host helper setup found in inspected OS module/package references.','Auth-payload UAF is serious; default tenant path unresolved until helper/auth-context prerequisites are established. Upstream fixed at inclusive .95 boundary.'),
('63824','default_user_with_owned_key','include','KEYS, ASYMMETRIC_KEY_TYPE, ASYMMETRIC_PUBLIC_KEY_SUBTYPE, X509_CERTIFICATE_PARSER and CRYPTO_RSA=y. keyctl not denied by default seccomp. Own searchable asymmetric public key supports PKEY_ENCRYPT route without initial-userns capabilities; private-key PKCS8 parser is m but not needed for every affected operation.','Heap output-buffer OOB write/read in keyctl asymmetric operation. Fixed in .95; include as boundary fix, not claim .95 affected.'),
('98503','default_tenant_admin','borderline','AF_PACKET explicitly preloaded; namespace CAP_NET_RAW permits TX_RING. Socket payload/fragments can remain shared after early completion. Same baseline gate as other TX_RING defects; no extra host interface needed.','Primary text proves early ring-slot reuse/payload ownership violation. Effect beyond attacker-owned packet data and a distinct kernel integrity/escape primitive remains for impact review; do not automatically equate it to arbitrary kernel write.'),
('74517','default_kvm_feature_hardware','include_hardware_condition','KVM feature defaults on, delegated /dev/kvm. KVM/Intel/AMD modules built; source hardware-config generator adds vendor module on vmx/svm. Tenant VMM can create irqchip/vCPUs, run guest and destroy VM. No nested VMX or special physical I/O device required. Actual virtualization support/module/device permissions are runtime facts.','Delayed IOAPIC EOI work reaches freed vCPU; shared-kernel UAF. Default feature availability is distinct from proof that every compute/storage node runs a vulnerable KVM path.'),
('89929','intel_nested_kvm','include_hardware_condition','Tenant-controlled KVM VMM; Intel VMX CPU/module with nested virtualization and VPID enabled. kvm_intel nested defaults true in reviewed source. Attacker can run L1/L2 and drive INVVPID/migration inside its VM; no initial-userns capability check substitutes for these hardware/runtime prerequisites.','Stale translation after wrong-pCPU invalidation. Do not infer cross-VPS success solely from stale-TLB mechanism.'),
('89930','intel_nested_kvm','include_hardware_condition','Same Intel nested-VMX prerequisite; tenant VMM/guest can control failed/successful nested VM-entry and virtual VPID changes. Actual nested/VPID controls and CPU feature exposure unknown.','Skipped TLB flush on failed VM-entry; stale guest translations. The scope of memory reached depends on the complete nested/KVM state, not CVSS alone.'),
('89932','intel_nested_kvm','include_hardware_condition','Same Intel nested-VMX/VPID support. L1 can perform VMXOFF/VMXON within its VM and reuse nested VPID; hardware CPU migration/VPID reuse remains runtime-dependent.','Primary fix explicitly says stale TLB entries may come from a different vCPU or completely different VM; strongest stated cross-VM isolation consequence of this three-fix group. No vpsAdminOS reproduction performed.'),
('98720','intel_nested_kvm_evmcs','include_hardware_condition','KVM_HYPERV=y. Tenant VMM enables KVM_CAP_HYPERV_ENLIGHTENED_VMCS through ordinary vCPU KVM_ENABLE_CAP; nested_enable_evmcs sets its flag without initial-userns capability. Requires Intel VMX/nested and eVMCS use; running the host under Hyper-V is not the same prerequisite as enabling guest eVMCS.','Primary defect permits L2/L1-proxy access to L0 TPR due stale MSR bitmap. Explicit guest-to-host register boundary violation; full node-root/cross-VPS code execution is not demonstrated by that register access alone.'),
('74753','default_user_perf','include','PERF_EVENTS=y; source perf_event_paranoid defaults 2. Per-task events excluding kernel profiling are allowed without CAP_PERFMON; default seccomp allows perf_event_open. Own event groups/exec/fd lifecycle suffice. Effective sysctl/LSM policy unknown.','EXIT leader UAF. Package B records supported 6.12 affected interval .96–.107, fixed .108; do not mark .95 affected merely because perf is enabled.'),
('93817','hardware_conditional_user_perf','include_hardware_condition','CPU_SUP_INTEL=y builds Intel PT pmu (arch/x86/events/intel/Makefile pt.o); pt_init checks actual X86_FEATURE_INTEL_PT. Own per-task exclude_kernel events/filter/inherit/fork allowed at upstream paranoid2, without host CAP_PERFMON; no dedicated CONFIG_INTEL_PT symbol should be invented. Actual PT PMU and policy unknown.','addr_filter_ranges freed while RCU paths read/write ranges. Hardware capability qualification; ordinary software perf events alone do not reach address-filter implementation.'),
('74662','optional_tenant_network_config','include','IPv4/IPv6 fragment core built; namespace fragment timeout sysctls registered per netns and writable by namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN. ipfrag_time parser has no positive minimum, so tenant can select zero then drive local fragment input. Default timeouts positive.','Timer before hash publication leaves stale fragment queue; not host-only despite nondefault timeout.'),
('74705','optional_tenant_network_config','include','UDP tunnel segmentation core available; preloaded vxlan/udp_tunnel, delegated TUN and AF_PACKET permit tenant-admin-controlled encapsulated/nonlinear traffic and own tunnel configuration. Needs pull-induced skb head relocation, not arbitrary UDP traffic.','Stale UDP header after pull reallocates skb head; concrete potential UAF. No platform-specific weaponization verified.'),
('80725','optional_tenant_network_config','include','Software GRO/TCP/IPv4/IPv6 built. Device gro_max_size defaults GRO_LEGACY_MAX_SIZE; tenant namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN can raise GRO_MAX_SIZE for own device through rtnetlink and arrange suitable veth/TUN/AF_PACKET traffic. Needs >64KiB aggregation plus insufficient pre-MAC room/nonplain protocol condition.','Pre-head memmove OOB write is concrete; BIG TCP is opt-in tenant network configuration, not universal default receive behavior.'),
('89478','optional_tenant_sctp_addip','include','SCTP preloaded. Removed-transport path needs an association, authenticated ASCONF DEL-IP/ADDIP and concurrent socket-backlog/direct receive handling. Per-netns addip/auth controls are tenant-admin writable; defaults off.','Transport restored into last_data_from after removal, later SACK UAF. No unconfigured Internet exposure claim.'),
('89479','tenant_sctp_endpoint','include','SCTP preloaded; requires matching endpoint/association handshake and bundled chunks on socket backlog. Distinct from ADDIP-only bugs: this described COOKIE ECHO/SHUTDOWN/ACK path does not establish an ADDIP/auth toggle requirement. Tenant can create own listener/peers using ordinary sockets.','Freed transport last_time_heard write and association UAF after same-packet deletion. Shared-kernel memory corruption, not demonstrated platform host root.'),
('98586','tenant_sctp_endpoint','include','SCTP preloaded; association/transport timer firing/rearm versus cleanup, plus proto-unreachable variant. Generic SCTP socket lifecycle, no ADDIP requirement established by primary description. Own sockets/peer traffic/close can exercise lifecycle.','Rearming timer before acquiring reference permits freed-object refcount operations. No platform-specific exploit verified.'),
('72463','optional_tenant_xfrm_config','include','XFRM_USER/INTERFACE=y and ESP/IPv4/IPv6 XFRM built; namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN configures states/interfaces. VTI drivers are m/unpreloaded, but built-in xfrmi_rcv_cb also assigns skb->dev, so source is not exclusive to operator-loaded VTI. Needs asynchronous resumption plus device replacement/teardown.','Device-reference imbalance and UAF; tenant-configured XFRM interface path plausible. Actual crypto async path/state/traffic remain candidate-specific prerequisites.'),
('98229','optional_tenant_xfrm_config','include','XFRM_USER/INTERFACE=y, namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN control. VTI needs modules, but built-in XFRM interface cross-netns callback or XFRM_MAX_DEPTH error can reset secpath without VTI. Tenant can control own nested network namespaces/state deletion.','State protocol/type dereference after final secpath reference reset is a concrete UAF. Configuring depth/receive/callback sequence is required; generic arbitrary inbound packet is insufficient.'),
('98368','optional_tenant_xfrm_config','include','INET_ESP/INET6_ESP=y, XFRM configuration namespace-scoped; needed AES/GCM paths built. Requires managed zerocopy frags on an out-of-place ESP output path. io_uring and relevant user operations pass default seccomp, but effective io_uring and crypto selection must be checked before deployment conclusions.','Mismatched managed-page ownership causes UAF/refcount loss and page leak; do not attribute every ESP output to this particular path.'),
('98369','optional_tenant_xfrm_config','include','XFRM transport-mode reinjection path built and PREEMPT_RCU=y in exact historical config. Requires workqueue-deferred receive packet with unpinned destination/device and concurrent namespace/device/route lifetime change; namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN can control its network lifecycle.','Missing RCU/dst/device references; warning evidence and lifetime risk, not proof of controlled host code execution. Introduction/range is owned by B stable join.'),
('98370','optional_tenant_xfrm_compat','include','XFRM_USER_COMPAT=y and IA32_EMULATION/COMPAT=y; compat ALLOCSPI and receiver path available to a 32-bit process under default seccomp. XFRM netlink control requires namespace CAP_NET_ADMIN, not initial-userns privilege. No xfrm_compat module load gate in this exact build.','Compat translation attaches/frees shared skb child, races receiver copy (UAF plus four-byte overread). Requires compat messages and multicast/receiver arrangement.')]
rows=[]
for short,group,decision,gate,impact in entries:
 cve='CVE-2026-'+short;r=records[cve];rows.append({'cve':cve,'title':r['title'],'stable_fixes':[{'sha':f['sha'],'release':f['release']} for f in r['fixes']],'group':group,'research_recommendation':decision,'source_gate':gate,'impact_limit':impact,'runtime_status':'not collected; source gate is not deployed proof','cna_url':r['cna_url']})
(out/'followup-candidate-gates.json').write_text(json.dumps({'recorded_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'source_linux':'a2384967b90f24d2470c9eb15f0e66d938df7e08','source_vpsadminos':'87fc13aac3fc8ce3d6c71c7ef3a8e72a5993a088','scope':'Candidate gates only, no exploit tests or live evidence','rows':rows},indent=2)+'\n')
p=root/'platform-baseline.md';s=p.read_text();old='IPv6 tunnel ICMP stale HAO metadata causes swap beyond inner packet into skb_shared_info. IPV6_MIP6=m compiles helper but ip6_tunnel module is not in default preload and autoload defaults off; valid HAO/XFRM prerequisites can also need mip6 type support. Conditional host module availability, then tenant-configured tunnel/traffic; no default exposure claim.';new='IPv6 tunnel ICMP stale HAO metadata causes swap beyond inner packet into skb_shared_info. Exact IPV6_TUNNEL=y is built in (corrected from an earlier module assumption). IPV6_MIP6=m compiles HAO helpers; successful processing of outer HAO needs a valid matching XFRM type/state, whose mip6 type module is absent from default preload/autoload off. Conditional MIP6 availability plus tenant-configured tunnel/traffic; no default exposure claim.';s=s.replace(old,new)
join=out/'coverage-later-cve-join.json';j=json.loads(join.read_text());target=next(x for x in j if x['current_cve_matches'] and x['current_cve_matches'][0]['cve']=='CVE-2026-74597');target['impact_and_gate']=new;join.write_text(json.dumps(j,indent=2)+'\n')
section='''## Follow-up candidate gates

This bounded follow-up covers the lead/architect's additional IDs. [Per-CVE JSON](platform-evidence/followup-candidate-gates.json) retains exact stable SHA/version, primary record, source gate and recommendation for every row. The same pinned historical configuration and current source-default limitations apply. Recommendations assess source-backed platform relevance; final selection/impact reconciliation belongs to architect/lead. No live runtime facts or exploitation tests were added.

| CVE (2026 prefix) | First fix | Gate / research disposition | Impact limit |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
'''
for r in rows:section+='| '+r['cve'].replace('CVE-2026-','')+' | '+', '.join(sorted(set(x['release'] for x in r['stable_fixes'])))+' | **'+r['research_recommendation'].replace('_',' ')+'**: '+r['source_gate']+' | '+r['impact_limit']+' |\n'
section+='''
For BPF 98041, the erroneous pointer prediction is reachable before the final pointer-comparison prohibition, but that is not equivalent to bypassing the alternate speculative-path verification. The mitigation conditions are preserved explicitly. For KVM eVMCS, guest capability enablement is distinct from the host-under-Hyper-V acceleration setting. For keys, a built-in public asymmetric parser is distinct from an unregistered encrypted key module or missing request-key helper authorization context. For XFRM, initial-user-namespace privilege is not required for namespace-scoped states/interfaces, but interface type, compat mode, crypto and lifetime prerequisites remain material.

'''
assert '## Follow-up candidate gates' not in s;s=s.replace('## Limits and next evidence',section+'## Limits and next evidence');p.write_text(s)
assert len(json.loads((out/'followup-candidate-gates.json').read_text())['rows'])==25
assert 'Exact IPV6_TUNNEL=y is built in' in p.read_text();print('VERIFIED follow-up rows',len(rows),'baseline bytes',p.stat().st_size)
